From: Doze-off <viniciussadxxx@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 00:13:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] SurfaceFlinger: Skip setColorTransform on primary display to fix blank screen

Some HWC HAL implementations do not support setColorTransform on the
primary display and respond with incorrect behavior, causing the display
to go blank after SurfaceFlinger attempts to apply a color transform.

Skip the setColorTransform call entirely when the target is the primary
display, returning NO_ERROR to avoid triggering the broken HAL path.

This is a workaround for devices/GSIs where the primary display HAL
does not implement color transform support.

Change-Id: Icd97c1973a2b2e7e9f8d6b784ff987662c8eca4b
---
 services/surfaceflinger/DisplayHardware/HWComposer.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/DisplayHardware/HWComposer.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/DisplayHardware/HWComposer.cpp
index f732d25d64..d7b72b480c 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/DisplayHardware/HWComposer.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/DisplayHardware/HWComposer.cpp
@@ -774,7 +774,12 @@ status_t HWComposer::setActiveModeWithConstraints(
 
 status_t HWComposer::setColorTransform(HalDisplayId displayId, const mat4& transform) {
     RETURN_IF_INVALID_DISPLAY(displayId, BAD_INDEX);
-
+    
+    if (displayId == getPrimaryDisplayId()) { 
+     LOG_DISPLAY_ERROR(displayId, "SKIP! Not implemented for primary display."); 
+     return NO_ERROR; 
+     } 
+    
     auto& displayData = mDisplayData[displayId];
     auto error = displayData.hwcDisplay->setColorTransform(transform);
     RETURN_IF_HWC_ERROR(error, displayId, UNKNOWN_ERROR);
